# Source Dependencies

Application dependencies flow toward composition:

```text
packages/*
    ^
source/components
    ^
source/providers / source/blocks
    ^
source/pages / source/router
    ^
source/app.tsx / source/main.tsx
```

## Rules

- `packages/*` never imports from `source/*`.
- `source/components` may consume packages, but not feature blocks, routes, or providers.
- `source/blocks` may consume packages, local components, and provider hooks through typed contracts.
- `source/pages` composes blocks and owns route guards.
- Use `@/` for source imports and `@sync/*` for shared packages.
- Keep feature data in the nearest `<name>.auth.constants.ts`.
- Keep form validation in `<name>.auth.schema.ts` and infer types from the schema.
- Keep API transport/domain types in `packages/api-client` or `packages/types`, not JSX files.
- Keep styles in role-specific `*.styles.ts` files and constants in role-specific `*.constants.ts` files.
- Use named exports and local `index.ts` boundaries; avoid default exports except where the application entry requires one.
- Run `pnpm typecheck:web` after browser-facing source changes.
